## 2. Function Byte-Length Specifications — FIPS 203 Grounding

These theorems restate the byte-length postconditions of each
function from `incremental_mlkem768_functions.txt`, annotated with
their FIPS 203 algorithm justification. Each theorem refers to the
existing spec theorem in the Lean spec tree (already proved) and
adds the FIPS 203 formula as a side-condition.

### T2.1: `generate` (F2) — ML-KEM.KeyGen (FIPS 203 Alg. 19)

```lean
/-- **`generate` byte-length postcondition grounded in FIPS 203 Alg. 19**.

`spqr::incremental_mlkem768::generate` implements ML-KEM.KeyGen
(Algorithm 19), which invokes ML-KEM.KeyGen_internal (Algorithm 16)
to produce (ek, dk) with:
  |ek| = 384·k + 32 = 1184, decomposed as pk1 (64) + pk2 (1152)
  |dk| = 768·k + 96 = 2400

The existing `generate_spec` in `Generate.lean` proves:
  generate ⦃ (result : Keys × R) =>
    result.1.hdr.length = 64     -- pk1 = ρ‖H(ek), FIPS 203 Alg. 13/16
    ∧ result.1.ek.length = 1152  -- pk2 = ByteEncode₁₂(t̂), Alg. 13 line 10
    ∧ result.1.dk.length = 2400  -- dk = dk_PKE‖ek‖H(ek)‖z, Alg. 16 line 3
  ⦄

FIPS 203 size consistency:
  64  = |ρ| + |H(ek)| = 32 + 32              (incremental)
  1152 = 384·k = 384·3                        (Table 3)
  2400 = 768·k + 96 = 768·3 + 96             (Table 3)

FIPS 203 §: §7.1, Alg. 19 → Alg. 16 → Alg. 13; Table 3
Cross-ref: Plan_incremental_mlkem768_I §2a
Functions: spqr::incremental_mlkem768::generate
-/
theorem generate_fips203_sizes :
    64 = 32 + 32
    ∧ (1152 : ℕ) = 384 * mlkem768_k
    ∧ (2400 : ℕ) = 768 * mlkem768_k + 96 := by
  constructor <;> [decide; constructor <;> decide]
```

### T2.2: `encaps1` (F3) — ML-KEM.Encaps Phase 1 (FIPS 203 Alg. 20, first half)

```lean
/-- **`encaps1` byte-length postcondition grounded in FIPS 203 Alg. 20**.

`spqr::incremental_mlkem768::encaps1` implements the first phase of
ML-KEM.Encaps (Algorithm 20), which runs ML-KEM.Encaps_internal
(Algorithm 17) and the first portion of K-PKE.Encrypt (Algorithm 14,
lines 1–21). It produces:
  c₁ ∈ 𝔹^(32·dᵤ·k) = 𝔹^960         (Alg. 14 line 22)
  encapsulation state ∈ 𝔹^2080        (libcrux internal encoding)
  shared secret K ∈ 𝔹^32              (Alg. 17 line 1)

The existing `encaps1_spec` in `Encaps1.lean` proves:
  encaps1 ⦃ (result : (Vec U8 × Vec U8 × Vec U8) × R) =>
    result.1.1.length = 960          -- c₁ = 32·dᵤ·k
    ∧ result.1.2.1.length = 2080     -- state = k·n·2 + n·2 + 32
    ∧ result.1.2.2.length = 32       -- K ∈ 𝔹³²
  ⦄

FIPS 203 size consistency:
  960  = 32·dᵤ·k = 32·10·3                   (Alg. 14 line 22)
  2080 = k·n·2 + n·2 + 32 = 1536 + 512 + 32  (libcrux; Alg. 14)
  32   = |K| ∈ 𝔹³²                           (Alg. 17 line 1)

FIPS 203 §: §7.2, Alg. 20 → Alg. 17 → Alg. 14 lines 1–21
Cross-ref: Plan_incremental_mlkem768_I §2b
Functions: spqr::incremental_mlkem768::encaps1
-/
theorem encaps1_fips203_sizes :
    (960 : ℕ) = 32 * mlkem768_dᵤ * mlkem768_k
    ∧ (2080 : ℕ) = mlkem768_k * mlkem768_n * 2 + mlkem768_n * 2 + 32
    ∧ (32 : ℕ) = 32 := by
  constructor <;> [decide; constructor <;> decide]
```

